{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "framework": "playwright",
  "testId": "testim-migrated/tests/webstore/checkout/validate-group-product-order-summary-section-for-guest-user.spec.ts > Webstore - Checkout > validate group product order summary section for guest user",
  "scenario": {
    "summary": "Guest adds a grouped product (qty 3), checks out as guest, edits the shipping address and adds a separate billing address, selects Custom Flat Rate shipping, checks the product name in the order summary, applies a voucher (Amount To Be Paid math), checks invalid voucher and coupon messages, applies a valid coupon (order-total math), fills additional info and places a COD order.",
    "steps": [
      "Open the webstore as a guest.",
      "addProductOfAnyType(groupProduct, 3); open the cart; Checkout as Guest; fill the guest address.",
      "Edit the shipping address (names, phone, street, postal code, city, email), untick 'same as billing', save; edit/add the billing address and save.",
      "Select Ship Complete + Custom Flat Rate; check productNameLink(groupProductId) contains groupProductName.",
      "Apply voucherNumber: voucher row number, Voucher Amount / Amount To Be Paid labels, order total - voucher = amount to be paid; remove the voucher.",
      "Apply an invalid voucher and an invalid coupon: error messages.",
      "Apply the coupon: success message, discount visible, Handling Charges, order-total math.",
      "Fill cart name and additional info, select COD, place the order, check the thank-you banner."
    ],
    "entitiesTouched": [
      "product",
      "coupon",
      "voucher",
      "shipping",
      "payment",
      "cart",
      "order"
    ],
    "stateChanges": [
      "Guest cart filled with the grouped product",
      "A guest order is placed (COD) with the edited shipping and billing addresses and the coupon; one coupon redemption is used"
    ],
    "assertions": [
      "'Proceed to Checkout', 'Shipping Address' and 'Billing Address' headings",
      "productNameLink(groupProductId) contains groupProductName",
      "Voucher row equals voucherNumber; Voucher Amount / Amount To Be Paid labels; |order total - voucher - to be paid| <= 0.05",
      "Invalid voucher / invalid coupon messages",
      "Coupon success message; discount visible; Handling Charges label; order-total math within 0.05",
      "ADDITIONAL INFO heading; thank-you banner"
    ],
    "evidence": [
      "Title and the five step labels match the flow; guest storageState.",
      "groupProduct z-2200003, groupProductId 408, groupProductName: tda rows shows PimProductId 408, active GroupedProduct 'Speedaire Positive Displacement Blower/Vacuum Pump'. PRODUCT_GROUPED_IN_STOCK quantityUsed 3, outputs sku, productId, name.",
      "coupon TestimTestCoupon25: tda rows shows an Amount Off Order coupon of store MaxwellsHardware (PortalId 7), discount 25, order minimum 10, coupon required, allowed with other coupons, no profile; mapped to COUPON_AMOUNT_OFF_ORDER (collection, creates a fresh coupon per run; output couponCode). The test does not assert the discount amount (only the totals math read from the page).",
      "DOUBT: the asserted coupon success message ('- Coupon successfully applied.') may be the promotion's PromotionMessage (the recorded coupon's message is 'Coupon successfully applied'); the COUPON_AMOUNT_OFF_ORDER collection creates 'Coupon Applied Successfully'. If the page shows the promotion message, this assertion depends on the coupon data. The approved cart coupon entries (ORDER15, message 'Coupon Applied Successfully', asserted 'Coupon applied successfully.') suggest the page shows a fixed resource string instead.",
      "Re-mapped (voucher keys 2026-11-01): voucherNumber E2O43NF74Y -> need voucher (VOUCHER_UNRESTRICTED), output voucherNumber, preferred (the test's own voucher first); read-only: applied and removed, no order placed with it",
      "checkoutPage.selectShippingMethod clicks Ship Complete and then lblShippingMethodFLAT (Custom Flat Rate): SHIPPING_FLAT_RATE_ON_STORE, shippingCode FLAT. tda rows: ZnodeShipping FLAT is Custom, DestinationCountryCode US, so countries 'us' (the address itself is masked).",
      "selectCOD/codRadio pays with COD (txtCOD): PAYMENT_COD_ON_STORE. No source carries the COD code the page object uses, so the need has no data source.",
      "Profile (atstage 2026-10-31) has no observations for the checkout specs: every source is profiled false. Values were checked read-only with `tda rows` where noted.",
      "Store MaxwellsHardware: the store every migrated webstore spec runs on (as in the approved shopping-cart and PDP entries); not named in the scan.",
      "Initial, edited shipping and billing address values (masked) are typed into the guest order: created-by-test.",
      "couponAmount is in the spec's schema but not in the scan values (unused by the spec).",
      "swap: data only through loadData (groupProduct -> product.sku, groupProductId -> product.productId, groupProductName -> product.name, coupon -> coupon.couponCode, voucherNumber -> voucher.voucherNumber), no derived assertions (totals read from the page, 0.05 tolerances, fixed UI text), no data value in the spec code (z-2200003 appears only in comments), no other data file. The voucher is removed before the order is placed.",
      "2026-11-01 run evidence: migrate, not swap - COUPON_AMOUNT_OFF_ORDER is created by its collection; the expected coupon message wraps the original coupon promotion message (\"- Coupon successfully applied.\"), the created coupon shows \"Coupon applied successfully\" (normal run tda-playwright-1793504829267). Rule 3: an expected value depends on the record."
    ],
    "confidence": "low",
    "needsReview": true
  },
